{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort | xargs -r -I{} sh -c \\\"printf 'FILE %s\\\\n' '{}' ; sed -n '1,220p' '{}'\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"FILE /workspace/README.md\n# ClickHouse live schema migration\n\nThis workspace adds `region` to `analytics.events` without downtime.\n\nMigration approach:\n\n- `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` is metadata-only in ClickHouse, so reads and writes continue while the schema changes.\n- The new column uses a deterministic `DEFAULT` expression derived from `user_id`, so existing rows return a non-empty `region` immediately after the column is added.\n- `MATERIALIZE COLUMN region` backfills existing parts asynchronously so the values are persisted on disk as well.\n\nThe migration SQL lives in `migrations/001_add_region_to_events.sql`.\nFILE /workspace/migrations/001_add_region_to_events.sql\nALTER TABLE analytics.events\n    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS region LowCardinality(String)\n    DEFAULT multiIf(\n        startsWith(user_id, 'u1_'), 'us-east',\n        startsWith(user_id, 'u2_'), 'eu-west',\n        startsWith(user_id, 'u3_'), 'ap-south',\n        'unknown'\n    );\n\nALTER TABLE analytics.events\n    MATERIALIZE COLUMN region;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
